Q: How to Cancel Previous API Calls When Updating Query Params in Angular with TanStack Query A: <p>Per your STR, I assume that query params changes in URL are observed via route observable that updates some signal connected to TanStack query flow.</p>
<p>As you didn't provide minimum code example I've forked TanStack's public one, to demonstrate problem and solutions. It may differ in some ways, but the core concept should be the same.</p>
<p><strong>Canceling problem</strong> (<a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/tanstack-query-nt8par8d?file=src%2Fapp%2Fcomponents%2Fpost.component.ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer">stackblitz</a>)</p>
<p>Every time <code>queryKey</code> change, we send a new request without canceling the previous one.</p>
<pre class="lang-ts prettyprint-override"><code>  // assume that `this.postId()` rapidly changes
  readonly postQuery = injectQuery(() =&gt; ({
    enabled: this.postId() &gt; 0,
    queryKey: ['post', this.postId()],
    queryFn: () =&gt; {
      return lastValueFrom(this.#postsService.postById$(this.postId()));
    },
  }));
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Direct abort signal solution</strong> (<a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/tanstack-query-ftk1qi8w?file=src%2Fapp%2Fcomponents%2Fpost.component.ts&amp;preset=node" rel="nofollow noreferrer">stackblitz</a>)</p>
<p>To solve the problem we'll utilize the <code>context.signal</code> abort signal. Per <a href="https://tanstack.com/query/latest/docs/framework/angular/guides/query-cancellation" rel="nofollow noreferrer">docs</a> it states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>When a query becomes out-of-date or inactive, this signal will become aborted.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Every time <code>queryKey</code> changes, the abort signal will be triggered, and we can use it to cancel previous request.</p>
<pre class="lang-ts prettyprint-override"><code>  // canceling with `context.signal` directly in component
  readonly postQuery = injectQuery(() =&gt; ({
    enabled: this.postId() &gt; 0,
    queryKey: ['post', this.postId()],
    queryFn: (context) =&gt; {
      const abort$ = fromEvent(context.signal, 'abort');

      return lastValueFrom(
        this.#postsService.postById$(this.postId()).pipe(takeUntil(abort$))
      );
    },
  }));
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Abstracted abort signal solution</strong> (<a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/tanstack-query-mywy3vzk?file=src%2Fapp%2Fservices%2Fposts-service.ts&amp;preset=node" rel="nofollow noreferrer">stackblitz</a>)</p>
<p>I'm not a big fan of mixing API service flow with components. So, if you want to commit to TanStack and leave space for Angular's <a href="https://angular.dev/guide/signals/resource" rel="nofollow noreferrer">resources</a>/<a href="https://angular.dev/ecosystem/rxjs-interop#using-rxresource-for-async-data" rel="nofollow noreferrer">rxResources</a> I recommend abstracting <code>injectQuery</code> to service and exposing only signals similar to what you would do with <code>httpClient</code> and observables. This will allow you to reuse entire flows via service in multiple components and scale/maintain logic easily.</p>
<pre class="lang-ts prettyprint-override"><code>  // canceling with `context.signal` from service method
  postById(
    postId: number | Signal&lt;number&gt;,
    destroyTriggers?: DestroyTriggers
  ): CreateQueryResult&lt;Post, Error&gt; {
    if (!isSignal(postId)) {
      postId = signal(postId);
    }

    const createAborters = abortFactory(destroyTriggers);

    return injectQuery(() =&gt; ({
      enabled: postId() &gt; 0,
      queryKey: ['post', postId()],
      queryFn: (context) =&gt; {
        const aborters$ = createAborters(context.signal);

        return lastValueFrom(
          this.#http
            .get&lt;Post&gt;(`https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/${postId()}`)
            .pipe(takeUntil(aborters$))
        );
      },
    }));
  }
</code></pre>

Q: How to show continued numbered of data with pagination A: <p>Try to set the <code>row_number</code> to <code>$start+1</code> instead of <code>0</code> on the model, so it will not start from 0 again on every page requested :  </p>

<pre><code>$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;query('set @row_number = '.$start+1);
</code></pre>
